Keep PLAY_BILLING_ENABLED unset/false. Do not enable billing.

Problem: eas.json production and preview already bundle
  EXPO_PUBLIC_SUBSCRIPTION_PURCHASE_ENTRY_ENABLED=1
  EXPO_PUBLIC_QUOTA_UPSELL_ENABLED=1
so the Upgrade sheet can be visible. Tapping purchase still calls
prepareAndroidBillingAccount / prepareIOSBillingAccount, which fail-closed
when PLAY_BILLING_ENABLED / APPSTORE_BILLING_ENABLED are not "true".
iapSession then returns kind:"failed" and does not call requestPurchase.
Users can see an unavailable purchase experience.

Proposed public-release behavior (config only):
  eas.json build.production.env and build.preview.env:
    remove or set to "" (not "1"):
      EXPO_PUBLIC_SUBSCRIPTION_PURCHASE_ENTRY_ENABLED
      EXPO_PUBLIC_QUOTA_UPSELL_ENABLED
  Leave PLAY_BILLING_ENABLED and APPSTORE_BILLING_ENABLED false.

Effect:
  UI visibility: quota upsell and Settings upgrade closed (gate_off /
  purchase_entry_closed).
  Store-request dispatch: still unreachable while prepare fails, and now
  also unreached from those entry points.
  Charge / server verify / entitlement: unchanged (already fail-closed).

Do not change IAP session retry logic or entitlement writes.
